{"@context":{"lean":"lean:","block":"block:","imports":{"@type":"@id"}},"@graph":[{"@id":"lean:module:QOU.Knot.HomflySkeinReference","@type":"LeanModule","name":"QOU.Knot.HomflySkeinReference","imports":["lean:module:Init","lean:module:Mathlib.Tactic.Ring","lean:module:Mathlib.Tactic.FieldSimp","lean:module:Mathlib.Tactic.NormNum"],"declarations":7,"chunks":1},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Knot.HomflySkeinReference.plain_inversion_eq_mirror_at_three","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Knot.HomflySkeinReference.plain_inversion_eq_mirror_at_three","kind":"theorem","line":118,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Knot/HomflySkeinReference.lean#L118-L124","doc":"At `k = 3`, by contrast, they *do* agree — the accident, stated so it is\non the record next to the `k = 2` refutation rather than discovered again. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Knot.HomflySkeinReference.plain_inversion_ne_mirror","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Knot.HomflySkeinReference.plain_inversion_ne_mirror","kind":"theorem","line":109,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Knot/HomflySkeinReference.lean#L109-L116","doc":"**The `z`-sign is not optional.** Inverting `v` alone is *not* the mirror:\nat `v = 2, z = 1` the naive substitution and the true mirror disagree already\nat `k = 2`. The agreement one sees at `k = 3` is an artefact of `z` occurring\nthere only as `z²`, and must not be read as a rule. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Knot.HomflySkeinReference.engine_k3_is_mirror","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Knot.HomflySkeinReference.engine_k3_is_mirror","kind":"theorem","line":101,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Knot/HomflySkeinReference.lean#L101-L107","doc":"**The engine's `k = 3` entry is the reference at the mirror.**\n`homflypt_2strand` returns `−v⁻⁴ + 2v⁻² + v⁻²z²` labelled \"Right-hand\ntrefoil\"; that is `skein` at `(v⁻¹, −z)`, i.e. the *left*-handed trefoil. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Knot.HomflySkeinReference.engine_k2_is_mirror","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Knot.HomflySkeinReference.engine_k2_is_mirror","kind":"theorem","line":91,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Knot/HomflySkeinReference.lean#L91-L99","doc":"**The engine's `k = 2` entry is the reference at the mirror.**\n`homflypt_2strand` returns `v⁻³z⁻¹ − v⁻¹z⁻¹ − v⁻¹z` labelled \"Hopf link\n(positive)\"; that is `skein` evaluated at `(v⁻¹, −z)`, i.e. the *negative*\nHopf link. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Knot.HomflySkeinReference.skein_three","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Knot.HomflySkeinReference.skein_three","kind":"theorem","line":81,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Knot/HomflySkeinReference.lean#L81-L89","doc":"The right-handed trefoil. Note `v⁻¹` has vanished: the closed form is a\ngenuine polynomial, which is why `hv` is needed to get there. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Knot.HomflySkeinReference.skein_two","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Knot.HomflySkeinReference.skein_two","kind":"theorem","line":73,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Knot/HomflySkeinReference.lean#L73-L79","doc":"The positive Hopf link. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Knot.HomflySkeinReference.skein","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Knot.HomflySkeinReference.skein","kind":"def","line":62,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Knot/HomflySkeinReference.lean#L62-L69","doc":"The 2-strand skein recurrence for `P(closure(σ₁ⁿ))`, in the Lickorish\nconvention `v⁻¹P(L₊) − vP(L₋) = zP(L₀)`. Resolving one positive crossing gives\n`P(L₊) = v²P(L₋) + vzP(L₀)`; on `σ₁ⁿ` the switched diagram is `σ₁ⁿ⁻²` and the\nsmoothed one is `σ₁ⁿ⁻¹`. Seeds are the 2-component unlink and the unknot. ","signatureChunk":0}]}